  greetings:
  - Make it quick. I've got a shift.
  - You're the one June told me about.
  aboutSelf: Nights at the elevator in Barlow, days asleep, Sundays at church so June doesn't skin me. That's my whole life, Detective.
  aboutTown: I drive out of this town every night, and every night it's harder to come back. Like the road's longer on the way in.
  seenAnythingStrange: Back in June, coming home at dawn, I passed a fella walking the highway into town carrying a sample case. No car, no coat, nobody walks to Semblance. When I looked in the mirror there was nobody on the road.
  foundersDay: Slept through most of it. Woke up to rain on the church roof and Mae's cherry pie. That's all I need from a holiday.
  gossip:
  - title: About June Marsh
    response: June wears her ring on her left hand like a normal person. Not like the Thornes.
  - title: About Amos Calder
    response: Amos's mouth droops on the right. Stroke, maybe. He won't let Doc look at it.
